      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1909 the Dryden Fruit Growers Union formed, and the first fruit warehouse followed, sparking a boom in apple orchards.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dryden%2C_Washington",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Icicle Canal finished in 1913, providing irrigation that accelerated orchard planting throughout Dryden.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
